\ ==== the LFO: :lfo { :shape :rate :delay :fade :key-sync :pitch :cutoff :pan },
\      operator :lfo-level and :lfo-width ====

\ Each voice has one LFO. Its value l in [-1, 1] follows :shape at :rate Hz,
\ starting from phase 0 at note-on when :key-sync is 1 (the default) or from
\ the free-running clock's phase when 0. It acts only after :delay seconds,
\ then grows to full depth over :fade seconds. Destinations: pitch (+/-
\ :pitch semitones), cutoff (+/- :cutoff octaves), pan (+ :pan x l), an
\ operator's level (x 1 - :lfo-level (1 - l)/2, a tremolo) and a pulse's
\ width (+ :lfo-width x l). A square LFO holds each half-cycle, so most
\ checks compare its two halves.

11 seed

: amp ( v hz -- a ) 48000 swap amplitude-at 0.70710678 / ;
: span ( stereo start finish -- v ) | stereo start finish | stereo start 48000 * round finish 48000 * round 0 1 submatrix ;
: right-span ( stereo start finish -- v ) | stereo start finish | stereo start 48000 * round finish 48000 * round 1 2 submatrix ;
: r2 ( f -- f ) 100 * round 100 / 0 + ;
: play-for ( patch seconds -- stereo ) | patch seconds | silence patch 0 patch! :a4 1 0 note-on seconds render-audio ;
: up ( -- hz ) 440 2 1 12 / ^ * ;
: down ( -- hz ) 440 2 -1 12 / ^ * ;

\ === pitch: a square LFO holds +1 then -1 semitone ===
{ :lfo { :shape :square :rate 0.5 :pitch 1 } } 2 play-for to vibrato
vibrato 0.1 0.9 span up amp r2 . vibrato 1.1 1.9 span down amp r2 . cr      \ 1 1 (+1 semitone, then -1)
vibrato 0.1 0.9 span 440 amp 0.05 < . cr                                    \ 1 (not at the note itself)
clear

\ === shapes, from a full-depth tremolo sampled at eighths of a 2 Hz cycle ===
: tremolo ( shape -- stereo ) | shape | { } [ { :fixed 1000 :lfo-level 1 } ] :operators ! { } shape :shape ! 2 :rate ! :lfo ! 0.6 play-for ;
: level-at ( stereo cycle -- a ) | stereo cycle | stereo cycle 0.5 * 0.0025 - cycle 0.5 * 0.0025 + span 1000 amp ;
: trace ( shape -- ) | shape | shape tremolo to wave [ 0.125 0.25 0.375 0.625 0.75 ] ( wave swap level-at r2 . ) each cr ;
:sine trace                       \ 0.85 1 0.85 0.15 0 ((1 + sin)/2)
:triangle trace                   \ 0.75 1 0.75 0.25 0 (straight lines)
:saw trace                        \ 0.13 0.25 0.38 0.63 0.75 (a ramp from -1 to 1: the phase itself)
:square trace                     \ 1 1 1 0 0
clear

\ === sample-and-hold: one value per cycle, different each cycle ===
{ } [ { :fixed 1000 :lfo-level 1 } ] :operators ! { :shape :sample-and-hold :rate 2 } :lfo ! 1.6 play-for to held
held 0.05 0.2 span 1000 amp held 0.3 0.45 span 1000 amp - abs 0.02 < . cr   \ 1 (constant within a cycle)
held 0.3 0.45 span 1000 amp held 0.8 0.95 span 1000 amp - abs 0.02 > . cr   \ 1 (a new value the next cycle)
7 seed held  7 seed { } [ { :fixed 1000 :lfo-level 1 } ] :operators ! { :shape :sample-and-hold :rate 2 } :lfo ! 1.6 play-for = . cr   \ 0 (seed 11 and seed 7 differ)
clear

\ === :delay and :fade ===
{ :lfo { :shape :square :rate 0.5 :pitch 1 :delay 0.5 } } 1 play-for to delayed
delayed 0.05 0.45 span 440 amp r2 . delayed 0.55 0.95 span up amp r2 . cr    \ 1 1 (the note itself until 0.5 s)
{ :lfo { :shape :square :rate 0.5 :pitch 12 :fade 1 } } 1 play-for to fading
fading 0.45 0.55 span 440 2 0.5 ^ * amp 0.5 > . cr                          \ 1 (half way through the fade: half an octave up)
clear

\ === :key-sync: 1 starts at phase 0; 0 follows the clock ===
: late-note ( sync -- stereo ) | sync | silence { } { :shape :square :rate 1 :pitch 1 } sync :key-sync ! :lfo ! 0 patch!
	0.75 render-audio drop :a4 1 0 note-on 0.4 render-audio ;
1 late-note 0.05 0.35 span up amp r2 . cr          \ 1 (synced: the first half-cycle, +1 semitone)
0 late-note 0.05 0.2 span down amp r2 . cr          \ 1 (free: the clock is at phase 0.75, the second half)
clear

\ === cutoff and pan ===
{ :operators [ { :wave :saw } ] :cutoff 440 :lfo { :shape :square :rate 0.5 :cutoff 2 } } 2 play-for to wobble
wobble 0.1 0.9 span 1320 amp wobble 1.1 1.9 span 1320 amp / 100 > . cr     \ 1 (cutoff 1760 Hz, then 110 Hz)
{ :operators [ { :fixed 1000 } ] :lfo { :shape :square :rate 0.5 :pan 1 } } 2 play-for to swinging
swinging 0.1 0.9 span 1000 amp r2 . swinging 0.1 0.9 right-span 1000 amp r2 . cr   \ 0 1.41 (right only)
swinging 1.1 1.9 span 1000 amp r2 . swinging 1.1 1.9 right-span 1000 amp r2 . cr   \ 1.41 0 (then left only)
clear

\ === :lfo-level on a modulator moves the index, not the loudness of a plain carrier ===
{ :operators [ { :fixed 1000 } { :fixed 100 :lfo-level 1 } ] :modulation [ [ 1 0 2 ] ] :lfo { :shape :square :rate 0.5 } } 2 play-for to shimmer
shimmer 0.1 0.9 span 1100 amp r2 . shimmer 1.1 1.9 span 1100 amp r2 . cr    \ 0.58 0 (J1(2), then no modulation)
clear

\ === :lfo-width: a square becomes a 75% then a 25% pulse ===
{ :operators [ { :wave :pulse :fixed 1000 :lfo-width 0.25 } ] :lfo { :shape :square :rate 0.5 } } 2 play-for to widths
widths 0.1 0.9 span 2000 amp r2 . widths 1.1 1.9 span 2000 amp r2 . cr      \ 0.63 0.63 (even harmonics, absent from a square)
{ :operators [ { :wave :pulse :fixed 1000 } ] } 1 play-for 0.1 0.9 span 2000 amp r2 . cr   \ 0
silence clear

\ errors
{ :lfo { :shape :wobble } } 0 patch!               \ (unknown shape)
{ :lfo { :rate 0 } } 0 patch!                      \ (rate below 0.01 Hz)
{ :lfo { :pitch 25 } } 0 patch!                    \ (beyond two octaves)
{ :lfo { :key-sync 2 } } 0 patch!                  \ (not 0 or 1)
{ :lfo { :speed 1 } } 0 patch!                     \ (unknown key)
{ :operators [ { :lfo-width 0.5 } ] } 0 patch!     \ (width swing beyond 0.49)
